## Model card

[Official GLM-4.5 documentation](https://docs.z.ai/guides/llm/glm-4.5) explicitly lists GLM-4.5-Flash as the free reasoning/coding/agent member. [Official pricing](https://docs.z.ai/guides/overview/pricing) verifies **free input, cached input, cache storage and output**. The family interface is text input/output with thinking, function calling and structured output through Chat Completions. No Zen Free ID verified.

The family page advertises **128K context / 96K output**, but does not give a separate detailed Flash specification block. Treat that output limit as family-level documentation rather than an independently checked Flash endpoint limit. Exact Flash release date, cutoff and parameter count are unverified. The page's **355B/32B** and **106B/12B** counts explicitly describe GLM-4.5 and GLM-4.5-Air, respectively, and are not assigned to Flash. No exact-Flash open-weight license established.

### Raw benchmarks found

Three fresh searches returned substantial ordinary GLM-4.5 evidence but no sufficiently attributable Flash quality results. The official page's benchmark discussion is for GLM-4.5 and Air; neither family positioning nor free pricing verifies equal checkpoint performance.

A [community benchmark repository](https://github.com/mupengi-bot/glm-benchmark) lists Flash among its intended targets and describes model-judged coding, reasoning, Korean and math tests. Its fetched README contains methodology and an **example result schema for GLM-5.1**, not measured Flash results. No example values are treated as data.

No verified public exact-Flash GPQA, HLE, SWE-bench, Terminal-Bench, Tau2/Tau3, GDPval-AA, Claw-Eval or long-context retrieval score found. Native visual/audio capability is not claimed.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

Self-excluded pending exact-route benchmark evidence sufficient for quality scoring. Identity and free access are verified; missing evidence does not imply weak capability. No placeholder scores assigned.

